msgid "ui.tutorial.lesson1.title"
msgstr "Colony requests"

msgid "ui.tutorial.lesson1.body"
msgstr "Three resource requests are available at a time.\nDeliver resources to gain time and regalia.\nIf the timer reaches zero, the colony loses.\n\nYou need the same stock for requests and building.\nAnts pick nearby jobs with free slots."

msgid "ui.tutorial.lesson2.title"
msgstr "Paths and food"

msgid "ui.tutorial.lesson2.body"
msgstr "Paths speed up trips to work and home.\nTrees provide wood, quarries stone, and bushes food.\n\nAnts need food and a safe route to the canteen.\nA new nest adds five residents; they also need food.\nWorkplace load shows working+en route / slots."

msgid "ui.tutorial.lesson3.title"
msgstr "Build while paused"

msgid "ui.tutorial.lesson3.body"
msgstr "Press B to open construction. Space pauses or resumes the simulation independently.\nChoose a building and drag across tiles. A road and a building can share a tile.\nRight-click removes the latest addition on the selected tile. Ctrl+Z undoes a stroke. The cross cancels the whole plan. The triangle applies it."

msgid "ui.tutorial.lesson4.title"
msgstr "Camera and demolition"

msgid "ui.tutorial.lesson4.body"
msgstr "Use the wheel to zoom, and MMB, arrows or WASD to pan.\nIn construction, the Move tool lets you pan with LMB.\n\nThe Demolish tool marks buildings and roads for removal.\nRemoval happens when you apply the plan, with no refund.\nDemolishing a nest kills residents and needs confirmation.\nThe top menu offers settings, restart, and exit."

